<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Merged into the bundle's Info.plist at build time.

     Without a microphone usage description macOS will not raise the microphone
     prompt, and the Microphone pane in System Settings has no way to add an
     application by hand — so an app missing this key can never be granted access
     at all. A denied microphone is handed silence rather than an error, which is
     how this went unnoticed: recordings succeeded, transcribed the computer's
     side, and had digital zero where the voice should have been. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Local Whisper Transcriber records your voice so it can be transcribed on this machine. Nothing is uploaded.</string>
	<!-- The same trap, one list further down. Capturing the computer's own audio
	     with a Core Audio process tap is gated on System Audio Recording Only, and
	     without this key macOS has no sentence to put in the prompt, so it never
	     raises one: the tap is created, every status code says noErr, and the
	     capture delivers digital silence forever. Measured exactly that way from a
	     process that had no such key. -->
	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Local Whisper Transcriber records what your speakers are playing — the other side of your meeting — so it can be transcribed on this machine. Nothing is uploaded.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
